  "implementation": [
    "Only session.invite resolves Participant or Identity references to current members of the explicit Conversation under the ordinary Store resource authority. Other Participant assertions keep their own strict meaning.",
    "No implicit admission, unknown/foreign/revoked/removed member fallback or recipient-ceiling bypass. Distinct references resolving to the same Participant refuse before mutation.",
    "The original requested references stay in the immutable operation digest and exact peer proof. Replacing Identity with Participant syntax conflicts on the same logical operation; exact replay never reinvites.",
    "Current fresh invitations after explicit readmission capture the new membership epoch. The peer proof rejects substituting a Participant alias after admission and retains the exact current Session projection.",
    "Actual signed native and HTTP invitations and cross-transport original replay pass EdDSA/ES256. Typed HTTP reference documents the installed target forms and URI limit. Native admission deliberately collapses invalid target preflight to forbidden; HTTP reports invalid-request for duplicate aliases."
  ],
